---
import AppLayout from '../layouts/AppLayout.astro';
---

<AppLayout title="Solar in Hybrid Systems | OnLoop Energy" description="OnLoop Energy uses solar only as the daytime generation layer within a hybrid (wind + solar) architecture. We do not install solar-only systems. Learn why and how solar earns its place in a hybrid design.">
<div>
            

            


            


            {/* Hero Section */}
            <section class="hero hero--short">
                <div class="container">
                    <div class="hero__content">
                        <div class="hero__badge" style="margin-top: var(--space-12);">
                            <span class="hero__badge-dot"></span>
                            Solar: Within Hybrid Only
                        </div>
                        <h1 class="hero__title">Solar earns its place <span class="hero__title-highlight">as part of a hybrid</span>, not on its own.</h1>
                        <p class="hero__subtitle">OnLoop Energy uses solar — but only as the daytime generation layer within a wind + solar hybrid system. We do not install solar-only projects. Here is why, and how we use it.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <video poster="/images/stock/poster-solar.jpg" preload="none" class="hero__video" autoplay muted loop playsinline >
                    <source src="/images/stock/solar-hero.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
                </video>
            </section>

            {/* Solar Image Gallery */}
            <section class="content-section fade-in">
                <div class="container">
                    <div class="grid-2">
                        <div class="image-card image-card--large">
                            <img src="/images/stock/solar-farm-6619504_1920.webp" loading="lazy" alt="Solar panels as daytime generation layer in a hybrid wind and solar energy system" />
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            <span class="content-section__label">How We Use Solar</span>
                            <h2 class="content-section__title" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-8);">Solar as architecture, not a product
                            </h2>
                            <p class="content-section__text">Most energy companies sell solar because it is the easiest product to install and the simplest to market. We do not work that way.</p>
                            <p class="content-section__text">At OnLoop Energy, solar is deployed as the daytime generation component within a coordinated wind + solar hybrid architecture. It captures peak irradiance hours. Wind covers evenings, nights, and monsoon variability. Together, they deliver what solar alone cannot: 24/7 reliable generation for a C&I facility.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            {/* Section 1: Our View on Solar */}
            <section class="content-section content-section--light fade-in">
                <div class="container">
                    <div class="content-section__header" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-8);">
                        <span class="content-section__label">Our Position</span>
                        <h2 class="content-section__title">We do not install solar-only systems</h2>
                    </div>
                    <div class="grid-2" style="align-items: start;">
                        <div>
                            <p class="content-section__text">
                                Solar is a predictable, cost-effective daytime generation source — and it has earned its place in the energy mix. But for the C&I load profiles we serve, solar alone is structurally insufficient.
                            </p>

                            <p class="content-section__text">
                                A factory running three shifts needs power at 9pm and 3am. A processing plant consuming 2 MW continuously needs generation that tracks its load curve, not just daylight hours. Solar peaks from 10am to 3pm — leaving 17+ hours of grid dependency every day.
                            </p>

                            <p class="content-section__text">
                                This is not a criticism of solar. It is a statement of physics. And it is why we use solar only within a hybrid architecture where wind generation fills the gaps.
                            </p>

                        </div>
                        <div class="card" style="margin-top: -60px;">
                            <span class="card__number">01</span>
                            <div class="card__icon">
                                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                                    stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                                    <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="5" />
                                    <line x1="12" y1="1" x2="12" y2="3" />
                                    <line x1="12" y1="21" x2="12" y2="23" />
                                    <line x1="4.22" y1="4.22" x2="5.64" y2="5.64" />
                                    <line x1="18.36" y1="18.36" x2="19.78" y2="19.78" />
                                    <line x1="1" y1="12" x2="3" y2="12" />
                                    <line x1="21" y1="12" x2="23" y2="12" />
                                    <line x1="4.22" y1="19.78" x2="5.64" y2="18.36" />
                                    <line x1="18.36" y1="5.64" x2="19.78" y2="4.22" />
                                </svg>
                            </div>
                            <h4 class="card__title">The daytime foundation</h4>
                            <p class="card__text">
                                When designed with discipline, solar becomes the reliable daytime generation layer in a hybrid system. It provides cost-effective, predictable output during peak irradiance hours — while wind handles the rest.
                                With conservative degradation assumptions and hybrid-ready design from day one, a solar array within a hybrid system delivers decades of stable performance.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>  </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            {/* Section 2: How OnLoop Designs Solar */}
            <section class="content-section fade-in">
                <div class="container">
                    <div class="content-section__header">
                        <span class="content-section__label">How We Design</span>
                        <h2 class="content-section__title">How we design solar systems</h2>
                    </div>
                    <div class="grid-2">
                        <ul class="feature-list">
                            <li class="feature-item">
                                <div class="feature-item__icon">
                                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
                                        stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                                        <polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12" />
                                    </svg>
                                </div>
                                <span class="feature-item__text">Layouts designed around land, structures, shading, and access
                                    realities</span>
                            </li>
                            <li class="feature-item">
                                <div class="feature-item__icon">
                                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
                                        stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                                        <polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12" />
                                    </svg>
                                </div>
                                <span class="feature-item__text">Realistic performance assumptions that hold up over time</span>
                            </li>
                            <li class="feature-item">
                                <div class="feature-item__icon">
                                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
                                        stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                                        <polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12" />
                                    </svg>
                                </div>
                                <span class="feature-item__text">Focus on lifetime energy yield, not headline numbers</span>
                            </li>
                            <li class="feature-item">
                                <div class="feature-item__icon">
                                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
                                        stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                                        <polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12" />
                                    </svg>
                                </div>
                                <span class="feature-item__text">Designed to remain flexible for future hybrid
                                    integration</span>
                            </li>
                        </ul>
                        <div class="stats-grid" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: var(--space-6);">
                            <div class="stat-card stat-card--compact">
                                <div class="stat-card__icon">
                                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
                                        stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                                        <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" />
                                        <polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14" />
                                    </svg>
                                </div>
                                <div class="stat-card__value">25+</div>
                                <div class="stat-card__label">Design Life</div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="stat-card stat-card--compact">
                                <div class="stat-card__icon">
                                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
                                        stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                                        <path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14" />
                                        <polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01" />
                                    </svg>
                                </div>
                                <div class="stat-card__value">98%</div>
                                <div class="stat-card__label">Operational Reliability Target</div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="stat-card stat-card--compact">
                                <div class="stat-card__icon">
                                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
                                        stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                                        <polyline points="23 18 13.5 8.5 8.5 13.5 1 6" />
                                        <polyline points="17 18 23 18 23 12" />
                                    </svg>
                                </div>
                                <div class="stat-card__value">0.5%</div>
                                <div class="stat-card__label">Assumed Annual Degradation</div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="stat-card stat-card--compact">
                                <div class="stat-card__icon">
                                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
                                        stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                                        <polygon points="12 2 2 7 12 12 22 7 12 2"></polygon>
                                        <polyline points="2 17 12 22 22 17" />
                                        <polyline points="2 12 12 17 22 12" />
                                    </svg>
                                </div>
                                <div class="stat-card__value">100%</div>
                                <div class="stat-card__label">Hybrid-Ready by Design</div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            {/* Section 3: When Solar Makes Sense */}
            <section class="content-section content-section--light fade-in">
                <div class="container">
                    <div class="content-section__header">
                        <span class="content-section__label">Design Approach</span>
                        <h2 class="content-section__title">How solar fits within a hybrid design</h2>
                    </div>
                    <div class="grid-2">
                        <div>
                            <p class="content-section__text">
                                When we design a hybrid system, solar takes a defined and bounded role:
                            </p>
                            <ul class="feature-list mt-8">
                                <li class="feature-item">
                                    <div class="feature-item__icon">
                                        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
                                            stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"
                                            stroke-linejoin="round">
                                            <polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12" />
                                        </svg>
                                    </div>
                                    <span class="feature-item__text">Sized to the daytime load — not over-specified to compensate for missing wind</span>
                                </li>
                                <li class="feature-item">
                                    <div class="feature-item__icon">
                                        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
                                            stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"
                                            stroke-linejoin="round">
                                            <polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12" />
                                        </svg>
                                    </div>
                                    <span class="feature-item__text">Designed with shading, structural load, and land constraints fully accounted for</span>
                                </li>
                                <li class="feature-item">
                                    <div class="feature-item__icon">
                                        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
                                            stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"
                                            stroke-linejoin="round">
                                            <polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12" />
                                        </svg>
                                    </div>
                                    <span class="feature-item__text">Integrated at the grid interface with wind — shared cabling, protection, and metering where possible</span>
                                </li>
                                <li class="feature-item">
                                    <div class="feature-item__icon">
                                        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
                                            stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"
                                            stroke-linejoin="round">
                                            <polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12" />
                                        </svg>
                                    </div>
                                    <span class="feature-item__text">Modelled with conservative 0.5% annual degradation — no inflated projections</span>
                                </li>
                            </ul>
                            <p class="content-section__text mt-8">
                                If you have been told you need solar-only, we are happy to run an honest feasibility check on whether your site's load profile genuinely supports that decision.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card">
                            <div class="card__icon">
                                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                                    stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                                    <path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14" />
                                    <polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01" />
                                </svg>
                            </div>
                            <h4 class="card__title">Designed only within a hybrid context</h4>
                            <p class="card__text">
                                Every solar installation we design exists within a wider wind + solar architecture. We assess structural capacity, shading risks, and long-term load behavior before finalising the solar component's size or layout.
                                If the site data does not support a hybrid system with a genuine solar contribution, we will say so honestly — and not proceed.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            {/* CTA Section */}
            <section class="cta-section fade-in">
                <div class="container">
                    <div class="cta-section__content">
                        <h2 class="cta-section__title">Interested in a hybrid system for your C&I facility?</h2>
                        <p class="cta-section__text">Solar within a hybrid architecture delivers results that solar alone simply cannot. Talk to our team about whether your site's wind resource and load profile support a wind + solar hybrid.</p>
                        <div style="display: flex; gap: var(--space-4); flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center;">
                        <a href="/hybrid" class="btn btn--primary btn--large">
                            Explore Hybrid Systems
                            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                                stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" width="20" height="20">
                                <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12" />
                                <polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19" />
                            </svg>
                        </a>
                        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn--secondary btn--large">Talk to Our Team</a>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            



        </div>

</AppLayout>
